rule(r'void|nothingness|abyss|no end|dreamheart|rift|between times|dreamscapes|memories|genesis|creation|^age of', "Distance gathers around a small point of orientation, then loosens before it becomes a recognizable place. The edges of the `cspace`x have the wavering certainty of a remembered room. It's difficult to hold any one detail in view for long; something about the surroundings always seems to have just changed.")
rule(r'bridge|pier|boardwalk|dock|quay', 'A weathered span carries a worn line of passage above the supporting structure. Grit catches in the repeated joints, and small chips expose fresher material beneath the surface. The open footing gives nearby sounds room to travel, leaving the crossing feeling more exposed than the ground it connects.')
rule(r'\bwell\b(?!-)|fountain', 'Hands and weather have smoothed the upper edge of a `wstone rim`x. Farther down, the masonry keeps a rougher grain, with pale traces caught in the joints. The boundary invites a pause beside the feature, close enough to follow the little imperfections across the worn surface.', ('stone rim', 'The upper stone is broad and smoothed by weather and handling, cool against a resting palm. Shallow pits interrupt the worn edge, with room to lean together beside the masonry and look over the rim.'))
rule(r'plaza|square|courtyard|court|town center|city center|central hub', 'Hard ground opens into a broad public gathering space. Old repairs interrupt the surface, and the busiest patches have been worn smooth by crossing feet. Along the margins, small groups can find a little enclosure while the open center leaves every arrival plainly visible.')
rule(r'elevator|airlock', 'Close panels surround a small standing space, their repeated seams giving the compartment a precise, cramped shape. Fine scuffs cluster at shoulder and shoe height. The hard surfaces catch every rustle and breath, making even a brief pause feel separate from the larger structure around it.')
rule(r'ladder|crane|catwalk', 'Metal joints and narrow footing define this exposed framework. Rust catches around the fastenings, and the most handled edges show a brighter wear beneath the dull surface. With little room to move aside, every change of position brings the construction and the drop beyond it sharply into view.')
rule(r'boat|aboard|ship|sloop|freighter|ketch|airplane|\bbus\b|\btaxi\b|\btrain\b', 'A close structural shell encloses the passenger space. Repeated joints and fitted panels leave few wasted corners, their edges scuffed by the awkward business of settling in. The interior carries the stale fabric smell of travel, bringing nearby company within easy reach of a quiet conversation.')

